(function(E){ const x = E["exam-01"] = E["exam-01"] || {units:{}}; (x.units = x.units || {})["x01-r1"] = {"id":"x01-r1","patterns":["RA-history","GT1-notices","PARA-cause","PARA-rules"],"title":{"en":"Reading 1: Passage 1 / Section 1","tr":"Reading 1: Passage 1 / Section 1","fa":"Reading ۱: متن ۱ (Passage 1) / بخش ۱ (Section 1)"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to complete notes with words from a passage and to decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN by comparing one statement with one place in the text.","tr":"Bu derste notları metindeki kelimelerle tamamlamayı ve bir ifadeyi metindeki tek bir yerle karşılaştırarak TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar vermeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری یادداشت‌ها را با کلمه‌های متن کامل کنی و با مقایسه‌ی هر جمله با یک جای مشخص در متن، بین TRUE، FALSE و NOT GIVEN تصمیم بگیری."},"objectiveGT":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to find facts quickly in everyday texts: answer short questions with up to three words from the text, and decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN.","tr":"Bu derste günlük metinlerde bilgiyi hızla bulmayı öğreneceksin: kısa soruları metinden en fazla üç kelimeyle cevaplayacak ve TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar vereceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری اطلاعات را در متن‌های روزمره سریع پیدا کنی: به سؤال‌های کوتاه با حداکثر سه کلمه از متن جواب بدهی و بین TRUE، FALSE و NOT GIVEN تصمیم بگیری."},"sessions":[["explain"],["drill"],["exit"]],"explain":{"title":{"en":"Reading Passage 1: a factual history","tr":"Reading Passage 1: gerçeklere dayalı bir tarih","fa":"Reading Passage 1: یک روایت تاریخی"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to complete notes with words from a passage and to decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN by comparing one statement with one place in the text.","tr":"Bu derste notları metindeki kelimelerle tamamlamayı ve bir ifadeyi metindeki tek bir yerle karşılaştırarak TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar vermeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری یادداشت‌ها را با کلمه‌های متن کامل کنی و با مقایسه‌ی هر جمله با یک جای مشخص در متن، بین TRUE، FALSE و NOT GIVEN تصمیم بگیری."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"13"},{"label":{"en":"Time","tr":"Süre","fa":"زمان"},"value":{"en":"20 min","tr":"20 dk","fa":"۲۰ دقیقه"}},{"label":{"en":"Words","tr":"Kelime","fa":"کلمه"},"value":"~800"}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: the Morozov collection","tr":"Bu sınav: Morozov koleksiyonu","fa":"این آزمون: مجموعه‌ی موروزوف"},"intro":{"en":"Academic Passage 1 is usually a clear factual account in time order, about history or the natural world. Learn the paraphrases on the card: the notes and statements never use the passage’s own words.","tr":"Academic Passage 1 genelde tarih ya da doğa hakkında, zaman sırasına göre açık bir anlatımdır. Karttaki eş anlamlıları öğren: notlar ve ifadeler metnin kendi kelimelerini asla kullanmaz.","fa":"Academic Passage 1 معمولاً روایتی روشن و واقعی به ترتیب زمان است، درباره‌ی تاریخ یا طبیعت. معادل‌های کارت را یاد بگیر: یادداشت‌ها و جمله‌ها هیچ‌وقت کلمه‌های خودِ متن را به کار نمی‌برند."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x01-r1-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["RA-history","PARA-cause"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-history","n":35,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 35 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 35’inde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۳۵ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"The story of two collectors","tr":"İki koleksiyoncunun hikâyesi","fa":"داستان دو مجموعه‌دار"},"asks":{"en":"A factual history in time order: a family, two brothers, how they built a collection and what happened to it later. Passage 1 is usually this kind of account, about history or nature, with notes and TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN.","tr":"Zaman sırasına göre gerçeklere dayalı bir tarih: bir aile, iki kardeş, bir koleksiyonu nasıl oluşturdukları ve sonra ona ne olduğu. Passage 1 genelde tarih ya da doğa üzerine bu türden bir anlatımdır; notlar ve TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN ile gelir.","fa":"یک روایت تاریخی به ترتیب زمان: یک خانواده، دو برادر، اینکه چطور یک مجموعه ساختند و بعداً چه بر سرش آمد. Passage 1 معمولاً همین نوع روایت است، درباره‌ی تاریخ یا طبیعت، با یادداشت و TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN."},"fields":["The family","The first collector","The second collector","How he bought","What happened after 1917","The collection today"],"words":[{"a":"became rich","b":"made its fortune","tr":"zengin oldu","fa":"ثروتمند شد"},{"a":"gave","b":"donated","tr":"bağışladı","fa":"اهدا کرد"},{"a":"started","b":"began / took up","tr":"başladı","fa":"شروع کرد"},{"a":"views of nature","b":"landscapes","tr":"manzara resimleri","fa":"نقاشی منظره"},{"a":"seldom","b":"rarely","tr":"nadiren","fa":"به‌ندرت"},{"a":"asked an artist to make","b":"commissioned","tr":"sipariş etti","fa":"سفارش داد"},{"a":"careful","b":"cautious / methodical","tr":"temkinli","fa":"محتاط"},{"a":"nationalised","b":"became state property","tr":"devletleştirildi","fa":"دولتی شد"},{"a":"split","b":"divided between","tr":"bölündü","fa":"تقسیم شد"},{"a":"not on show","b":"kept in storage","tr":"sergilenmiyor","fa":"در انبار، نه در نمایش"},{"a":"only by invitation","b":"only to guests he had invited","tr":"yalnızca davetle","fa":"فقط با دعوت"},{"a":"very popular","b":"among the most visited","tr":"çok popüler","fa":"خیلی پرطرفدار"}],"traps":[{"en":"A statement that compares two people (\"earned more than his brother\") is NOT GIVEN when the text gives figures for only one of them.","tr":"İki kişiyi karşılaştıran bir ifade (\"kardeşinden fazla kazandı\"), metin yalnızca birinin rakamlarını veriyorsa NOT GIVEN’dır.","fa":"جمله‌ای که دو نفر را مقایسه می‌کند («بیشتر از برادرش درآمد داشت»)، وقتی متن فقط عددهای یکی را می‌دهد، NOT GIVEN است."},{"en":"Order words decide TRUE or FALSE: first, at first, later, within a few years, by 1900.","tr":"Sıra bildiren kelimeler TRUE ya da FALSE’u belirler: first, at first, later, within a few years, by 1900.","fa":"کلمه‌های ترتیب TRUE یا FALSE را تعیین می‌کنند: first، at first، later، within a few years، by 1900."},{"en":"The notes use other words than the passage (a general word for a specific one), but the answer itself is copied from the passage.","tr":"Notlar metinden farklı kelimeler kullanır (özel bir kelime yerine genel bir kelime), ama cevabın kendisi metinden aynen alınır.","fa":"یادداشت‌ها کلمه‌های دیگری به کار می‌برند (یک کلمه‌ی کلی به جای یک کلمه‌ی دقیق)، اما خودِ جواب عیناً از متن برداشته می‌شود."}],"example":{"text":"\"The library was founded in 1850. At first it lent books only to its members, but in 1872 it opened its doors to everyone.\"","item":"Statement: In its first years, anyone could borrow books from the library. TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","answer":"FALSE","why":{"en":"\"At first\" = in its first years; \"only to its members\" is the opposite of anyone.","tr":"\"At first\" = ilk yıllarında; \"yalnızca üyelerine\" \"herkes\"in tersi.","fa":"«at first» یعنی سال‌های اول؛ «فقط به اعضا» برعکسِ «هر کسی» است."}}},{"id":"RA-history-p1","ctx":["RA-history"],"title":{"en":"The history of an object, a place or a trade","tr":"Bir nesnenin, yerin ya da ticaretin tarihi","fa":"تاریخچه‌ی یک شیء، یک مکان یا یک تجارت"},"asks":{"en":"The history of an everyday object, a trade, a building or a discovery: where it began, who developed it, how it spread and how it changed. Statements test dates, people and causes; the notes follow the order of events.","tr":"Gündelik bir nesnenin, bir ticaretin, bir binanın ya da bir keşfin tarihi: nerede başladığı, kimin geliştirdiği, nasıl yayıldığı ve nasıl değiştiği. İfadeler tarihleri, kişileri ve nedenleri sınar; notlar olayların sırasını izler.","fa":"تاریخچه‌ی یک شیء روزمره، یک تجارت، یک ساختمان یا یک کشف: از کجا شروع شد، چه کسی آن را توسعه داد، چطور گسترش یافت و چطور تغییر کرد. جمله‌ها تاریخ‌ها، آدم‌ها و علت‌ها را می‌سنجند؛ یادداشت‌ها ترتیب رویدادها را دنبال می‌کنند."},"fields":["The material was first used by local farmers.","The design changed in the 18th century.","The inventor made a lot of money from it.","Notes: Origins · Early uses · Spread · Later developments"],"words":[{"a":"invented","b":"developed / came up with","tr":"icat etti","fa":"اختراع کرد"},{"a":"popular","b":"in demand / widely used","tr":"rağbet gören","fa":"پرطرفدار"},{"a":"spread","b":"was taken to / reached","tr":"yayıldı","fa":"گسترش یافت"},{"a":"expensive","b":"costly / only the rich could afford it","tr":"pahalı","fa":"گران"},{"a":"replaced","b":"took the place of / gave way to","tr":"yerini aldı","fa":"جایش را گرفت"},{"a":"soon","b":"within a few years / shortly afterwards","tr":"kısa sürede","fa":"به‌زودی"},{"a":"earlier than","b":"predates / came before","tr":"... -den önce","fa":"زودتر از"},{"a":"made money","b":"profited from / earned","tr":"para kazandı","fa":"پول درآورد"},{"a":"the government","b":"the authorities / the state","tr":"hükümet","fa":"دولت"},{"a":"exported","b":"sold abroad","tr":"ihraç etti","fa":"صادر کرد"},{"a":"remained","b":"continued / was still","tr":"kaldı, sürdü","fa":"باقی ماند"},{"a":"by hand","b":"without machines / manually","tr":"elle","fa":"با دست"}],"traps":[{"en":"NOT GIVEN when the text names a person but says nothing about their money, motives or feelings.","tr":"Metin bir kişinin adını verip parası, amacı ya da duyguları hakkında hiçbir şey söylemiyorsa: NOT GIVEN.","fa":"وقتی متن اسم کسی را می‌آورد ولی درباره‌ی پول، انگیزه یا احساسش چیزی نمی‌گوید: NOT GIVEN."},{"en":"Dates close together: \"first described in 1565, made in factories from 1795\". Match the date to the event.","tr":"Yakın tarihler: \"ilk kez 1565’te tarif edildi, 1795’ten itibaren fabrikada üretildi\". Tarihi olayla eşleştir.","fa":"تاریخ‌های نزدیک هم: «اولین بار ۱۵۶۵ توصیف شد، از ۱۷۹۵ در کارخانه ساخته شد». تاریخ را با رویداد جور کن."}],"example":{"text":"Glass windows were known in Roman times, but for centuries only churches and the very rich could afford them. In 1696 England introduced a tax on windows, and many owners bricked theirs up. The tax was finally abolished in 1851.","item":"Notes: Window tax: introduced in ___   (ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER)","answer":"1696","why":{"en":"1696 is when it was introduced; 1851 is when it was abolished.","tr":"1696 getirildiği yıl; 1851 kaldırıldığı yıl.","fa":"۱۶۹۶ سال وضع مالیات است؛ ۱۸۵۱ سال لغو آن."}},"track":"academic","general":true,"patterns":["RA-history"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-history","n":35,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 35 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 35’inde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۳۵ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Notes first, then six statements","tr":"Önce notlar, sonra altı ifade","fa":"اول یادداشت‌ها، بعد شش جمله"},"body":{"en":"Questions 1-7: complete notes with ONE WORD ONLY from the passage. Questions 8-13: TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN. Both sets follow the order of the passage. Spend about 20 minutes, because there is no extra time to copy answers.","tr":"Soru 1-7: notları metinden YALNIZCA BİR KELİMEYLE tamamla. Soru 8-13: TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN. İki grup da metnin sırasını izler. Yaklaşık 20 dakika ayır; cevapları aktarmak için ek süre yok.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۱ تا ۷: یادداشت‌ها را فقط با یک کلمه از متن کامل کن. سؤال‌های ۸ تا ۱۳: TRUE، FALSE یا NOT GIVEN. هر دو گروه به ترتیب متن جلو می‌روند. حدود ۲۰ دقیقه وقت بگذار، چون زمان اضافه برای انتقال جواب‌ها نیست."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Four steps","tr":"Dört adım","fa":"چهار قدم"},"steps":[{"en":"Read the note headings and find the same section in the passage: names and dates are your anchors.","tr":"Not başlıklarını oku ve metinde aynı bölümü bul: isimler ve tarihler çapandır.","fa":"عنوان یادداشت‌ها را بخوان و همان بخش را در متن پیدا کن: اسم‌ها و تاریخ‌ها لنگرت هستند."},{"en":"Read the words around each gap, find their paraphrase, and copy one word exactly.","tr":"Her boşluğun etrafındaki kelimeleri oku, eş anlamlısını bul ve tek bir kelimeyi aynen kopyala.","fa":"کلمه‌های دور هر جای خالی را بخوان، معادلشان را پیدا کن و یک کلمه را دقیقاً کپی کن."},{"en":"For each statement, find the one sentence it is about, and compare every detail.","tr":"Her ifade için ilgili olduğu tek cümleyi bul ve her ayrıntıyı karşılaştır.","fa":"برای هر جمله، همان یک جمله‌ی مربوط در متن را پیدا کن و همه‌ی جزئیات را مقایسه کن."},{"en":"Watch the small words: first, only, more than, rarely, always.","tr":"Küçük kelimelere dikkat et: first, only, more than, rarely, always.","fa":"حواست به کلمه‌های کوچک باشد: first، only، more than، rarely، always."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","tr":"FALSE mı NOT GIVEN mı?","fa":"FALSE یا NOT GIVEN؟"},"table":{"headers":{"en":["The text","The answer"],"tr":["Metin","Cevap"],"fa":["متن","جواب"]},"rows":[["says the same thing in other words","TRUE"],["says the opposite, or a different fact on the same point","FALSE"],["says nothing about this point","NOT GIVEN"]]}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One statement, step by step","tr":"Bir ifade, adım adım","fa":"یک جمله، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Do the following statements agree with the information given in the passage?","text":"\"The museum opened in 1902. At first it showed only local artists, but within ten years it had become known across Europe.\"","item":"Statement: The museum showed foreign artists from the day it opened.","answer":"FALSE","walk":[{"en":"Find the place: \"At first it showed...\"","tr":"Yeri bul: \"At first it showed...\"","fa":"جایش را پیدا کن: «At first it showed...»"},{"en":"Compare: \"only local artists\" at first, so not foreign artists from the start.","tr":"Karşılaştır: ilk başta \"yalnızca yerel sanatçılar\", yani en baştan yabancı sanatçılar değil.","fa":"مقایسه کن: اوایل «فقط هنرمندان محلی»، پس از روز اول هنرمند خارجی نبود."},{"en":"The text says the opposite: FALSE, not NOT GIVEN.","tr":"Metin tersini söylüyor: NOT GIVEN değil, FALSE.","fa":"متن برعکسش را می‌گوید: FALSE، نه NOT GIVEN."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Text: \"She published three novels.\" Statement: \"Her first novel was the most successful.\" TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"The text gives the number of novels, but says nothing about success.","tr":"Metin roman sayısını veriyor ama başarı hakkında hiçbir şey söylemiyor.","fa":"متن تعداد رمان‌ها را می‌گوید، اما درباره‌ی موفقیت چیزی نمی‌گوید."}},"remember":{"en":"One statement, one place in the text: same meaning TRUE, opposite FALSE, nothing NOT GIVEN.","tr":"Bir ifade, metinde bir yer: aynı anlam TRUE, ters FALSE, hiçbir şey NOT GIVEN.","fa":"یک جمله، یک جای متن: همان معنی TRUE، برعکس FALSE، هیچ NOT GIVEN."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x01-r1-e","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-01","unit":"x01-r1"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"Academic Reading Passage 1","title":{"en":"The Morozov brothers and their collection","tr":"Morozov kardeşler ve koleksiyonları","fa":"برادران موروزوف و مجموعه‌شان"},"timed":20,"ctx":["RA-history"],"intro":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.","passage":"The Morozov brothers and their collection\n\nIn the early years of the twentieth century, two of the finest collections of modern French painting in the world were being put together not in Paris, London or New York, but in Moscow. One belonged to the merchant Sergei Shchukin. The other was built by two brothers, Mikhail and Ivan Morozov, whose family had made its fortune in the textile industry. Their story shows how private taste can shape what later generations see on the walls of public museums.\n\nThe Morozovs had risen remarkably fast. The founder of the family business had been born a serf, legally tied to the land of his master, and had bought his freedom. Within three generations his descendants had become some of the richest industrialists in Russia, and their mills employed thousands of workers. Wealth of this kind brought new social expectations. Like other leading merchant families in Moscow, the Morozovs were expected to support public life, and members of the family paid for theatres, hospitals and schools.\n\nMikhail, the elder brother, was the first to collect seriously. He was a lively, sociable figure who also wrote about history and liked to fill his house with guests. In the 1890s he began buying works by Russian artists, and on visits to Paris he added paintings by French artists who were still regarded as experimental in Moscow. His collecting lasted barely a decade. He died in 1903 at the age of thirty-three, and some years later his widow donated his pictures to the Tretyakov Gallery, the city's main museum of Russian art.\n\nIvan, the younger brother, had a very different temperament. Quiet and methodical, he had studied chemistry in Zurich before returning to manage the family's factory in Tver, a town to the north-west of Moscow. He began collecting in about 1903, at first concentrating on Russian landscapes. Within a few years, however, his interest had turned almost entirely to France.\n\nWhat set Ivan Morozov apart from many other buyers was his patience. He rarely bought at auction. Instead, he worked closely with a small number of Paris dealers, and he was prepared to wait, sometimes for years, until the right picture became available. He is said to have kept a space free on one wall for a long time, because he had not yet found a painting good enough to fill it.\n\nThe two Moscow collectors were often compared. Shchukin enjoyed taking risks and bought the most challenging work of the day, including dozens of paintings by the young Picasso. Morozov's taste was more cautious: he bought only a few works by Picasso and preferred pictures that seemed to him complete and balanced. Some observers at the time regarded him as the less adventurous of the two, but his collection is now often admired for the consistent quality of its pictures.\n\nMorozov was also unusual in commissioning work. For the music room of his Moscow mansion he asked the French painter Maurice Denis to produce a series of large panels telling the ancient story of Psyche, and Pierre Bonnard painted three wide views of the Mediterranean coast for the staircase. Commissions like these meant that the house itself, and not only the individual paintings in it, became a work of art.\n\nBy 1917 the collection included several hundred paintings and sculptures, among them some of the finest works of Cézanne, Gauguin, Van Gogh and Matisse in any collection. Yet few people saw them. Unlike Shchukin, who opened his house to visitors on Sundays, Morozov showed his pictures only to guests he had invited.\n\nThe revolution of 1917 changed everything. In 1918 the new government took the collection into state ownership. Remarkably, Ivan Morozov was asked to stay on as an assistant keeper of the paintings he had bought, and for a short time he showed visitors around the rooms of what had been his own home. In 1919 he left Russia with his family, and he died two years later, abroad.\n\nThe collection did not remain in one place for long. In the 1920s it was combined with Shchukin's paintings to form a museum of modern Western art in Moscow. In 1948, however, the authorities closed the museum, declaring that modern French painting was unsuitable for Soviet audiences. The works were divided between the Pushkin Museum in Moscow and the Hermitage in what was then Leningrad, and for years many of them were kept in storage.\n\nToday the paintings are among the most visited works in both museums, and exhibitions of the collection abroad have attracted very large crowds. It is a striking result for a man who preferred to look at his pictures in private.","groups":[{"instruction":"Questions 1-7. Complete the notes below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"note","notesTitle":"The Morozov brothers","questions":[{"n":1,"kind":"gap","prompt":"The Morozov family · its wealth came from the ___ industry","accept":["textile"],"limit":1,"evidence":"made its fortune in the textile industry","why":{"en":"\"Made its fortune in the textile industry\" = its wealth came from.","tr":"\"Servetini tekstil sektöründe yaptı\" = zenginliği oradan geldi.","fa":"«ثروتش را از صنعت نساجی به دست آورد» یعنی ثروتش از آن‌جا آمد."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":2,"kind":"gap","prompt":"The Morozov family · paid for theatres, hospitals and ___","accept":["schools"],"limit":1,"evidence":"paid for theatres, hospitals and schools","why":{"en":"The list in the passage ends with schools. Keep the plural.","tr":"Metindeki liste schools ile bitiyor. Çoğulu koru.","fa":"فهرست متن با schools تمام می‌شود. جمع را نگه دار."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":3,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Mikhail · also wrote about ___","accept":["history"],"limit":1,"evidence":"also wrote about history","why":{"en":"\"He... also wrote about history.\"","tr":"\"Ayrıca tarih hakkında yazdı.\"","fa":"«درباره‌ی تاریخ هم می‌نوشت»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":4,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Mikhail · after his death, his ___ gave his paintings to the Tretyakov Gallery","accept":["widow"],"limit":1,"evidence":"his widow donated his pictures","why":{"en":"\"His widow donated his pictures\": gave = donated.","tr":"\"Dul eşi resimlerini bağışladı\": gave = donated.","fa":"«همسرِ بیوه‌اش تابلوهایش را اهدا کرد»: gave یعنی donated."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":5,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Ivan · had studied ___ in Zurich","accept":["chemistry"],"limit":1,"evidence":"studied chemistry in Zurich","why":{"en":"\"He had studied chemistry in Zurich.\"","tr":"\"Zürih’te kimya okumuştu.\"","fa":"«در زوریخ شیمی خوانده بود»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":6,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Ivan · bought mainly through Paris ___ rather than at auction","accept":["dealers"],"limit":1,"evidence":"a small number of Paris dealers","why":{"en":"\"He rarely bought at auction. Instead, he worked closely with... Paris dealers.\"","tr":"\"Nadiren müzayededen aldı. Bunun yerine... Paris’teki sanat tüccarlarıyla çalıştı.\"","fa":"«به‌ندرت از حراج می‌خرید. در عوض با... دلال‌های پاریسی کار می‌کرد»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase","TR-plural"]},{"n":7,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Ivan · asked Maurice Denis to paint panels for the ___ room","accept":["music"],"limit":1,"evidence":"For the music room of his Moscow mansion","why":{"en":"\"For the music room of his Moscow mansion.\" \"room\" is printed.","tr":"\"Moskova’daki konağının müzik odası için.\" \"room\" yazılı.","fa":"«برای اتاق موسیقیِ عمارتش در مسکو». «room» چاپ شده."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 8-13. Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","qtype":"tfng","questions":[{"n":8,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Ivan Morozov started collecting before his brother did.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"Mikhail, the elder brother, was the first to collect seriously","why":{"en":"Mikhail \"was the first to collect seriously\", so Ivan did not start first.","tr":"Mikhail \"ciddi olarak koleksiyon yapan ilk kişiydi\"; yani Ivan önce başlamadı.","fa":"میخائیل «اولین کسی بود که جدی مجموعه جمع کرد»، پس ایوان اول شروع نکرد."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":9,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Ivan Morozov’s early purchases were mainly paintings of the Russian countryside.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"at first concentrating on Russian landscapes","why":{"en":"\"At first\" = early; \"concentrating on Russian landscapes\" = mainly paintings of the countryside.","tr":"\"At first\" = ilk zamanlarda; \"Rus manzaralarına yoğunlaşarak\" = çoğunlukla kır resimleri.","fa":"«at first» یعنی اوایل؛ «تمرکز روی منظره‌های روسیه» یعنی بیشتر نقاشیِ روستا و طبیعت."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":10,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Ivan Morozov paid higher prices for his paintings than Shchukin did.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"worked closely with a small number of Paris dealers","why":{"en":"The passage says how he bought (through dealers, patiently), not what he paid compared with Shchukin.","tr":"Metin nasıl aldığını söylüyor (sabırla, tüccarlar aracılığıyla), Shchukin’e göre ne ödediğini değil.","fa":"متن می‌گوید چطور می‌خرید (با حوصله، از طریق دلال‌ها)، نه اینکه در مقایسه با شوکین چقدر پول می‌داد."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF","TR-hedge"]},{"n":11,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Morozov owned more works by Picasso than Shchukin did.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"he bought only a few works by Picasso","why":{"en":"Shchukin bought \"dozens\"; Morozov \"only a few\". The text says the opposite.","tr":"Shchukin \"düzinelerce\" aldı; Morozov \"yalnızca birkaç\". Metin tersini söylüyor.","fa":"شوکین «ده‌ها» اثر خرید؛ موروزوف «فقط چندتا». متن برعکس را می‌گوید."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":12,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"After the collection became state property, Morozov continued to work with it for a time.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"was asked to stay on as an assistant keeper","why":{"en":"He \"was asked to stay on as an assistant keeper... for a short time\".","tr":"\"Kısa bir süre... yardımcı koruma görevlisi olarak kalması istendi.\"","fa":"از او خواستند «برای مدتی کوتاه... به‌عنوان دستیار نگهدار بماند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":13,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Artists outside the Soviet Union protested when the museum was closed in 1948.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"the authorities closed the museum","why":{"en":"The closure and its reason are given; nothing is said about protests abroad.","tr":"Kapanma ve nedeni veriliyor; yurt dışındaki protestolar hakkında hiçbir şey yok.","fa":"بسته شدن موزه و دلیلش آمده؛ درباره‌ی اعتراض در خارج چیزی گفته نشده."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]}]}],"id":"c-x01-r1-d","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-01","unit":"x01-r1"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"paraphrase","point":1,"prompt":"A note says \"gave his paintings to a museum\". Which word in a passage would you look for?","options":["purchased","donated","borrowed"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"To donate is to give something, often to a museum or charity.","tr":"Donate, genelde bir müzeye ya da hayır kurumuna bir şey vermektir.","fa":"donate یعنی چیزی را، اغلب به موزه یا خیریه، هدیه دادن."}},{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"He commissioned three panels for the staircase.\" This means he...","options":["asked an artist to make them for him","bought them at an auction","sold them to a museum"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"To commission a work is to ask and pay an artist to produce it.","tr":"Bir eseri commission etmek, bir sanatçıdan onu yapmasını isteyip ücretini ödemektir.","fa":"commission کردن یک اثر یعنی از هنرمند بخواهی آن را بسازد و پولش را بدهی."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"Notes say \"ONE WORD ONLY from the passage\". The passage says \"made its fortune in the textile industry\". The note is \"wealth came from the ___ industry\". You write...","options":["textiles","the textile","textile"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Copy the word exactly as it appears: textile.","tr":"Kelimeyi metinde geçtiği gibi aynen kopyala: textile.","fa":"کلمه را دقیقاً همان‌طور که در متن آمده کپی کن: textile."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Text: \"The garden was opened to the public in 1931.\" Statement: \"The garden was popular with visitors as soon as it opened.\"","options":["TRUE","NOT GIVEN","FALSE"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"The date of opening is given; popularity is not mentioned.","tr":"Açılış tarihi veriliyor; ne kadar sevildiğinden söz edilmiyor.","fa":"تاریخ بازگشایی آمده؛ از محبوبیتش حرفی نیست."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Text: \"She rarely gave interviews.\" Statement: \"She often spoke to journalists.\"","options":["FALSE","TRUE","NOT GIVEN"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"\"Rarely\" contradicts \"often\": FALSE.","tr":"\"Rarely\", \"often\" ile çelişiyor: FALSE.","fa":"«rarely» با «often» تناقض دارد: FALSE."}}],"id":"c-x01-r1-x","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-01","unit":"x01-r1"},"gt":{"explain":{"title":{"en":"GT Reading Section 1: everyday notices","tr":"GT Reading Section 1: günlük duyurular","fa":"GT Reading Section 1: اطلاعیه‌های روزمره"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to find facts quickly in everyday texts: answer short questions with up to three words from the text, and decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN.","tr":"Bu derste günlük metinlerde bilgiyi hızla bulmayı öğreneceksin: kısa soruları metinden en fazla üç kelimeyle cevaplayacak ve TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar vereceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری اطلاعات را در متن‌های روزمره سریع پیدا کنی: به سؤال‌های کوتاه با حداکثر سه کلمه از متن جواب بدهی و بین TRUE، FALSE و NOT GIVEN تصمیم بگیری."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"14"},{"label":{"en":"Texts","tr":"Metin","fa":"متن"},"value":"2"},{"label":{"en":"Word limit","tr":"Kelime sınırı","fa":"سقف کلمه"},"value":{"en":"3 words / number","tr":"3 kelime / sayı","fa":"۳ کلمه / عدد"}}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: a fun run and a hostel","tr":"Bu sınav: bir halk koşusu ve bir hostel","fa":"این آزمون: یک دوی همگانی و یک هاستل"},"intro":{"en":"Section 1 has short texts from daily life: notices, adverts, guides and reviews. The questions test details: times, prices, places and rules.","tr":"Section 1 günlük hayattan kısa metinler içerir: duyurular, ilanlar, rehberler ve yorumlar. Sorular ayrıntıları ölçer: saatler, fiyatlar, yerler ve kurallar.","fa":"Section 1 متن‌های کوتاهی از زندگی روزمره دارد: اطلاعیه، آگهی، راهنما و نظر مشتری. سؤال‌ها جزئیات را می‌سنجند: ساعت، قیمت، مکان و قانون."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x01-r1gt-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["GT1-notices","PARA-rules"],"often":{"pattern":"GT1-notices","n":22,"of":65,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 22 of the last 65 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 65 metnin 22’sinde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۲۲ متن از ۶۵ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"A race notice and a hostel guide","tr":"Bir yarış duyurusu ve bir hostel rehberi","fa":"اطلاعیه‌ی یک مسابقه و راهنمای یک هاستل"},"asks":{"en":"Section 1 gives two short everyday texts: information for people taking part in an event and rules for guests. The questions ask for times, places, prices and what is or is not allowed.","tr":"Section 1 iki kısa günlük metin verir: bir etkinliğe katılanlar için bilgiler ve misafirler için kurallar. Sorular saatleri, yerleri, fiyatları ve neyin serbest olup olmadığını sorar.","fa":"Section 1 دو متن کوتاه روزمره می‌دهد: اطلاعاتی برای شرکت‌کننده‌های یک رویداد و قوانینی برای مهمان‌ها. سؤال‌ها ساعت، مکان، قیمت و اینکه چه چیزی مجاز است یا نه را می‌پرسند."},"fields":["Entry and fees","Collecting a pack","Times","Rules","Charges","What is included"],"words":[{"a":"free","b":"at no extra cost / free of charge","tr":"ücretsiz","fa":"رایگان"},{"a":"not included","b":"is extra / costs £...","tr":"dahil değil","fa":"شامل نمی‌شود"},{"a":"must","b":"you will need to / every bag must","tr":"zorunda","fa":"باید"},{"a":"not allowed","b":"it is not possible to / cannot","tr":"izin yok","fa":"مجاز نیست"},{"a":"sold at","b":"on sale at / can be bought from","tr":"... satılır","fa":"فروخته می‌شود در"},{"a":"thrown away","b":"cleared out / disposed of","tr":"atılır","fa":"دور ریخته می‌شود"},{"a":"weekly","b":"once a week / every Friday","tr":"haftalık","fa":"هفتگی"},{"a":"store your bags","b":"leave your luggage","tr":"çantanı bırakmak","fa":"گذاشتن کیف‌ها"},{"a":"hire","b":"can be hired / rented","tr":"kiralamak","fa":"کرایه کردن"},{"a":"deadline","b":"entry closes at midnight on","tr":"son tarih","fa":"مهلت"}],"traps":[{"en":"\"On weekdays\" in the text and \"at weekends\" in the statement: one word of time makes it FALSE.","tr":"Metinde \"hafta içi\", ifadede \"hafta sonu\": tek bir zaman kelimesi onu FALSE yapar.","fa":"در متن «روزهای کاری» و در جمله «آخر هفته»: یک کلمه‌ی زمانی آن را FALSE می‌کند."},{"en":"Short answers: copy at most three words and/or a number from the text. \"your booking reference\" is three words; \"the number they sent you\" is not in the text.","tr":"Kısa cevaplar: metinden en fazla üç kelime ve/veya bir sayı al. \"your booking reference\" üç kelime; \"the number they sent you\" metinde yok.","fa":"جواب‌های کوتاه: حداکثر سه کلمه و/یا یک عدد از متن بردار. «your booking reference» سه کلمه است؛ «the number they sent you» در متن نیست."}],"example":{"text":"\"Towels can be hired from reception for £2 for your whole stay.\"","item":"How much does it cost to hire a towel?","answer":"£2","why":{"en":"One number, copied from the text.","tr":"Metinden alınmış tek bir sayı.","fa":"یک عدد، عیناً از متن."}}},{"id":"GT1-notices","ctx":["GT1-notices"],"title":{"en":"Notices, rules and FAQs","tr":"Duyurular, kurallar ve SSS","fa":"اطلاعیه، قانون و پرسش‌های متداول"},"asks":{"en":"Notices, rules and frequently asked questions for a service: a tram, a leisure centre, a block of flats, a competition. Questions test rules, conditions, dates and exceptions.","tr":"Bir hizmet için duyurular, kurallar ve sık sorulan sorular: tramvay, spor merkezi, apartman, yarışma. Sorular kuralları, koşulları, tarihleri ve istisnaları sınar.","fa":"اطلاعیه، قانون و پرسش‌های متداول برای یک خدمت: تراموا، مرکز ورزشی، یک ساختمان مسکونی، یک مسابقه. سؤال‌ها قانون‌ها، شرط‌ها، تاریخ‌ها و استثناها را می‌سنجند."},"fields":["Passengers must buy a ticket before boarding.","Children under five travel free.","Refunds are given for delays of over 30 minutes.","Residents may leave bicycles in the hallway."],"words":[{"a":"must","b":"are required to","tr":"zorunda","fa":"باید"},{"a":"not allowed","b":"prohibited / not permitted","tr":"yasak","fa":"ممنوع"},{"a":"within 14 days","b":"in less than two weeks","tr":"14 gün içinde","fa":"ظرف ۱۴ روز"},{"a":"can claim","b":"are entitled to / are eligible for","tr":"talep edebilir","fa":"می‌تواند درخواست کند"},{"a":"apply","b":"submit a form","tr":"başvurmak","fa":"درخواست دادن"},{"a":"proof","b":"a receipt / evidence of","tr":"kanıt","fa":"مدرک"},{"a":"residents","b":"people living in the building","tr":"sakinler","fa":"ساکنان"},{"a":"compensation","b":"money for a problem you had","tr":"tazminat","fa":"غرامت"},{"a":"beforehand","b":"in advance","tr":"önceden","fa":"از قبل"},{"a":"except","b":"apart from / with the exception of","tr":"hariç","fa":"به‌جز"},{"a":"responsible for","b":"must take care of","tr":"... -den sorumlu","fa":"مسئولِ"},{"a":"on request","b":"if you ask","tr":"talep üzerine","fa":"در صورت درخواست"}],"traps":[{"en":"Exceptions: \"all passengers must..., except season-ticket holders\". A statement about everyone may be FALSE.","tr":"İstisnalar: \"bütün yolcular ... zorunda, abonman sahipleri hariç\". Herkes hakkındaki bir ifade FALSE olabilir.","fa":"استثناها: «همه‌ی مسافران باید...، به‌جز دارندگان بلیت فصلی». جمله‌ای درباره‌ی همه ممکن است FALSE باشد."},{"en":"Numbers in conditions: \"30 minutes or more\" and \"over 30 minutes\" are not the same.","tr":"Koşullardaki sayılar: \"30 dakika veya daha fazla\" ile \"30 dakikadan fazla\" aynı değildir.","fa":"عددها در شرط‌ها: «۳۰ دقیقه یا بیشتر» با «بیش از ۳۰ دقیقه» یکی نیست."}],"example":{"text":"Delay Repay: if your train arrives 30 minutes or more late, you can claim 50% of your ticket price. Claims must be made within 28 days of travel.","item":"Statement: Passengers can claim the full price of their ticket.  (TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN)","answer":"FALSE","why":{"en":"The notice says 50%, which contradicts \"the full price\".","tr":"Duyuru %50 diyor; bu \"tam fiyat\" ile çelişiyor.","fa":"اطلاعیه می‌گوید ۵۰٪، که با «قیمت کامل» در تضاد است."}},"track":"gt","general":true,"patterns":["GT1-notices"],"often":{"pattern":"GT1-notices","n":22,"of":65,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 22 of the last 65 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 65 metnin 22’sinde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۲۲ متن از ۶۵ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Two texts, two tasks","tr":"İki metin, iki görev","fa":"دو متن، دو تمرین"},"body":{"en":"Questions 1-7 are about the first text: answer each question with NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the text. Questions 8-14 are TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN statements about the second text.","tr":"Soru 1-7 ilk metinle ilgili: her soruyu metinden EN FAZLA ÜÇ KELİME VE/VEYA BİR SAYIYLA cevapla. Soru 8-14 ikinci metinle ilgili TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN ifadeleridir.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۱ تا ۷ درباره‌ی متن اول‌اند: به هر سؤال با حداکثر سه کلمه و/یا یک عدد از متن جواب بده. سؤال‌های ۸ تا ۱۴ جمله‌های TRUE، FALSE یا NOT GIVEN درباره‌ی متن دوم‌اند."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Four steps","tr":"Dört adım","fa":"چهار قدم"},"steps":[{"en":"Use the headings of the text to find the right section fast.","tr":"Doğru bölümü hızla bulmak için metnin başlıklarını kullan.","fa":"برای پیدا کردن سریع بخش درست از عنوان‌های متن استفاده کن."},{"en":"Read the question word: where wants a place, when a time, how much a price.","tr":"Soru kelimesini oku: where bir yer, when bir zaman, how much bir fiyat ister.","fa":"کلمه‌ی پرسشی را بخوان: where مکان، when زمان، how much قیمت می‌خواهد."},{"en":"Copy the answer from the text; do not change its form.","tr":"Cevabı metinden kopyala; biçimini değiştirme.","fa":"جواب را از متن کپی کن؛ شکلش را عوض نکن."},{"en":"Count the words: \"the main entrance\" is three; \"12 June\" is a number and one word.","tr":"Kelimeleri say: \"the main entrance\" üç; \"12 June\" bir sayı ve bir kelime.","fa":"کلمه‌ها را بشمار: «the main entrance» سه کلمه است؛ «12 June» یک عدد و یک کلمه."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","tr":"FALSE mı NOT GIVEN mı?","fa":"FALSE یا NOT GIVEN؟"},"table":{"headers":{"en":["The text","The answer"],"tr":["Metin","Cevap"],"fa":["متن","جواب"]},"rows":[["says the same thing in other words","TRUE"],["says the opposite, or a different fact on the same point","FALSE"],["says nothing about this point","NOT GIVEN"]]}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One short answer, step by step","tr":"Bir kısa cevap, adım adım","fa":"یک جواب کوتاه، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Answer the question. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the text for each answer.","text":"\"Members can borrow up to six books at a time. DVDs must be returned within seven days.\"","item":"How long can members keep a DVD?","answer":"seven days","walk":[{"en":"\"How long\" asks for a length of time.","tr":"\"How long\" bir süre soruyor.","fa":"«how long» مدت زمان را می‌پرسد."},{"en":"Find DVDs: \"returned within seven days\".","tr":"DVD’leri bul: \"seven days içinde iade\".","fa":"DVDها را پیدا کن: «ظرف seven days برگردانده شوند»."},{"en":"Copy two words: seven days.","tr":"İki kelime kopyala: seven days.","fa":"دو کلمه کپی کن: seven days."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Text: \"Children under five swim free.\" Statement: \"Children under five must be with an adult.\" TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","options":["NOT GIVEN","TRUE","FALSE"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"The text is about the price, not about adults.","tr":"Metin fiyatla ilgili, yetişkinlerle değil.","fa":"متن درباره‌ی قیمت است، نه همراهی بزرگ‌ترها."}},"remember":{"en":"Find the section by its heading, then copy the answer exactly, inside the limit.","tr":"Bölümü başlığından bul, sonra cevabı sınırın içinde aynen kopyala.","fa":"بخش را از عنوانش پیدا کن، بعد جواب را دقیقاً و داخل سقف کلمه کپی کن."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x01-r1-e-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-01","unit":"x01-r1"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"General Training Reading Section 1","title":{"en":"A fun run and a youth hostel","tr":"Bir halk koşusu ve bir gençlik hosteli","fa":"یک دوی همگانی و یک هاستل جوانان"},"timed":20,"ctx":["GT1-notices"],"texts":[{"title":"Riverside 10K Fun Run: information for runners","kind":"notice","body":"The Riverside 10K takes place on Sunday 14 June. Please read this information carefully before the day.\n\nEntering the race\nOnline entry closes at midnight on 7 June, and it is not possible to enter on the day. The entry fee is £18, or £12 for runners under 18. Every runner who finishes receives a T-shirt and a medal.\n\nCollecting your race pack\nRace packs contain your race number and a timing chip, which you fix to your shoe. Packs can be collected from the Town Hall on Friday 12 June or Saturday 13 June, between 10 am and 6 pm. You will need to show the confirmation email, either printed or on your phone. We are sorry, but packs cannot be sent by post.\n\nOn the day\nThe start is in Victoria Park, beside the bandstand. Please arrive by 8.30 am, as the race starts promptly at 9.15. A bag store will be open in the large tent next to the start. Every bag must be labelled with your race number, and you are advised not to leave valuables in it.\n\nThe route\nThe course follows the riverside path for two laps and is almost completely flat. There are water stations at 3 km and 7 km. Roads along the route are closed for 90 minutes only; after that, anyone who has not finished will be asked to continue on the pavement.\n\nMedical help\nFirst-aid staff will be at the start, at both water stations and at the finish. If you feel unwell at any point, stop running and speak to one of the marshals, who will be wearing yellow jackets.\n\nRaising money\nEntry fees cover the cost of organising the event, but we hope runners will also collect money for the town's children's hospital. Anyone who raises more than £100 will receive a free photo of themselves crossing the finish line.\n\nGetting there\nThere is no parking at Victoria Park. Free shuttle buses run from the railway station every 15 minutes from 7.30 am."},{"title":"Harbourside Youth Hostel: guest guide","kind":"guide","body":"Welcome to Harbourside. This guide explains how things work here. If you have any questions, the reception desk is open 24 hours a day.\n\nArriving and leaving\nRooms are ready from 3 pm, and you must leave your room by 10 am on the day you go. If you arrive early or leave late, you can put your bags in the luggage room behind reception at no extra cost.\n\nYour key card\nYour key card opens the front door and your room. If you lose it, there is a £5 charge for a new one.\n\nThe guest kitchen\nThe kitchen is open from 7 am to 11 pm. Any food you keep in the fridge must have a label with your name and the date you are leaving. Food without a label is removed every morning when the kitchen is cleaned. If you prefer not to cook, breakfast is served in the café for £6.50; it is not included in the price of your room.\n\nBedding and towels\nClean sheets and pillowcases are provided, but towels are not. If you have forgotten yours, towels can be hired from reception for £2 for your whole stay.\n\nLockers\nThere is a locker under every bed. You will need your own padlock, and padlocks are on sale at reception.\n\nLaundry\nWashing machines are in the basement. Tokens cost £3 each from reception. The drying room next door is free to use.\n\nQuiet hours\nPlease keep noise to a minimum between 11 pm and 7 am. Groups of more than ten people who want to hold a social event should book the meeting room.\n\nWi-Fi\nWi-Fi is free throughout the building. The password changes every Monday and is shown on the screen at reception.\n\nBicycles\nBicycles can be hired from reception, and a helmet is included in the price. All bicycles must be returned by 8 pm."}],"groups":[{"text":0,"instruction":"Questions 1-7. Read the text below and answer Questions 1-7. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the text for each answer.","qtype":"short-answer","questions":[{"n":1,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Apart from a T-shirt, what does every runner who finishes receive? ___","accept":["a medal","medal"],"limit":3,"evidence":"a T-shirt and a medal","why":{"en":"\"Every runner who finishes receives a T-shirt and a medal.\"","tr":"\"Bitiren her koşucu bir tişört ve bir madalya alır.\"","fa":"«هر دونده‌ای که تمام کند یک تی‌شرت و یک مدال می‌گیرد»."},"trap":["TR-limit","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":2,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Apart from the race number, what is in the race pack? ___","accept":["a timing chip","timing chip"],"limit":3,"evidence":"your race number and a timing chip","why":{"en":"\"Race packs contain your race number and a timing chip.\"","tr":"\"Paketlerde yarış numaran ve bir zaman çipi var.\"","fa":"«بسته‌ها شامل شماره‌ی مسابقه و یک تراشه‌ی زمان‌سنج‌اند»."},"trap":["TR-limit","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":3,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Where can runners collect their race pack? ___","accept":["the Town Hall","Town Hall"],"limit":3,"evidence":"collected from the Town Hall","why":{"en":"\"Packs can be collected from the Town Hall.\"","tr":"\"Paketler Belediye Binası’ndan alınabilir.\"","fa":"«بسته‌ها را می‌شود از ساختمان شهرداری گرفت»."},"trap":["TR-limit","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":4,"kind":"gap","prompt":"What must runners show to collect their pack? ___","accept":["the confirmation email","confirmation email"],"limit":3,"evidence":"You will need to show the confirmation email","why":{"en":"Three words from the text: the confirmation email.","tr":"Metinden üç kelime: the confirmation email.","fa":"سه کلمه از متن: the confirmation email."},"trap":["TR-limit","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":5,"kind":"gap","prompt":"By what time should runners arrive at the start? ___","accept":["8.30 am","8.30"],"limit":3,"evidence":"Please arrive by 8.30 am","why":{"en":"9.15 is the start of the race; runners should arrive by 8.30 am.","tr":"9.15 yarışın başlangıcı; koşucular 8.30’a kadar gelmeli.","fa":"۹:۱۵ شروع مسابقه است؛ دونده‌ها باید تا ۸:۳۰ برسند."},"trap":["TR-limit","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":6,"kind":"gap","prompt":"For how long are the roads along the route closed? ___","accept":["90 minutes"],"limit":3,"evidence":"closed for 90 minutes only","why":{"en":"\"Roads along the route are closed for 90 minutes only.\"","tr":"\"Güzergâhtaki yollar yalnızca 90 dakika kapalı.\"","fa":"«جاده‌های مسیر فقط ۹۰ دقیقه بسته‌اند»."},"trap":["TR-limit","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":7,"kind":"gap","prompt":"What will runners who raise more than £100 receive? ___","accept":["a free photo","free photo","photo"],"limit":3,"evidence":"a free photo of themselves","why":{"en":"\"A free photo of themselves crossing the finish line\": three words are enough.","tr":"\"Bitiş çizgisini geçerken çekilmiş ücretsiz bir fotoğraf\": üç kelime yeter.","fa":"«یک عکس رایگان از خودشان هنگام عبور از خط پایان»: سه کلمه کافی است."},"trap":["TR-limit","TR-paraphrase"]}]},{"text":1,"instruction":"Questions 8-14. Do the following statements agree with the information given in the text? Write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","qtype":"tfng","questions":[{"n":8,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Guests who arrive before their room is ready can leave their luggage free of charge.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"put your bags in the luggage room behind reception at no extra cost","why":{"en":"\"At no extra cost\" = free of charge.","tr":"\"Ek ücret olmadan\" = ücretsiz.","fa":"«بدون هزینه‌ی اضافه» یعنی رایگان."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":9,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Breakfast is included in the price of the room.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"it is not included in the price of your room","why":{"en":"\"It is not included in the price of your room.\"","tr":"\"Oda fiyatına dahil değil.\"","fa":"«در قیمت اتاقت حساب نشده»."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":10,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Food without a label is thrown away each evening.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"Food without a label is removed every morning","why":{"en":"Removed every morning, not each evening.","tr":"Her akşam değil, her sabah kaldırılıyor.","fa":"هر صبح برداشته می‌شود، نه هر عصر."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":11,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Guests can buy a padlock at the hostel.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"padlocks are on sale at reception","why":{"en":"\"Padlocks are on sale at reception.\"","tr":"\"Asma kilitler resepsiyonda satılıyor.\"","fa":"«قفل‌ها در پذیرش فروخته می‌شوند»."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":12,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Most guests prefer to use the drying room rather than a dryer.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"The drying room next door is free to use","why":{"en":"The text says the drying room is free; it says nothing about what most guests prefer.","tr":"Metin kurutma odasının ücretsiz olduğunu söylüyor; misafirlerin çoğunun neyi tercih ettiğini söylemiyor.","fa":"متن می‌گوید اتاق خشک‌کن رایگان است؛ درباره‌ی ترجیح بیشتر مهمان‌ها چیزی نمی‌گوید."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF","TR-hedge"]},{"n":13,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"The Wi-Fi password is changed once a week.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"The password changes every Monday","why":{"en":"\"Every Monday\" = once a week.","tr":"\"Her pazartesi\" = haftada bir.","fa":"«هر دوشنبه» یعنی هفته‌ای یک بار."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":14,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Guests who stay longer pay less to hire a bicycle.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"Bicycles can be hired from reception","why":{"en":"Hiring and helmets are mentioned, but no prices for longer stays.","tr":"Kiralama ve kask söz konusu, ama uzun kalanlar için fiyat yok.","fa":"از کرایه و کلاه ایمنی حرف زده شده، ولی از قیمت برای اقامت طولانی نه."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]}]}],"id":"c-x01-r1-d-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-01","unit":"x01-r1"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"paraphrase","point":1,"prompt":"A statement says \"free of charge\". Which words in a notice mean the same?","options":["for a small fee","included in some cases","at no extra cost"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"\"At no extra cost\" = you do not pay anything more.","tr":"\"Ek ücret olmadan\" = fazladan bir şey ödemezsin.","fa":"«بدون هزینه‌ی اضافه» یعنی پول بیشتری نمی‌دهی."}},{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"In a guide for guests, \"removed\" food is food that is...","options":["cooked","taken away","sold"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"Removed = taken away from its place.","tr":"Removed = yerinden alınmış.","fa":"removed یعنی از جایش برداشته شده."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"\"Answer with NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER.\" Which answer is NOT acceptable?","options":["the old railway station","the station","90 minutes"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"\"the old railway station\" is four words: over the limit.","tr":"\"the old railway station\" dört kelime: sınırı aşıyor.","fa":"«the old railway station» چهار کلمه است: بیشتر از سقف."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Text: \"The pool is closed on Mondays.\" Statement: \"The pool is closed on Sundays.\"","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Careful: the text only tells you about Mondays. It does not say whether the pool opens on Sundays.","tr":"Dikkat: metin yalnızca pazartesileri söylüyor. Havuzun pazar açık olup olmadığını söylemiyor.","fa":"دقت کن: متن فقط درباره‌ی دوشنبه‌ها می‌گوید. نمی‌گوید استخر یکشنبه‌ها باز است یا نه."}}],"id":"c-x01-r1-x-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-01","unit":"x01-r1"}}}; })(globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS = globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS || {});
